= Description logic — Simple =

'''Description logics''' are formal languages for describing categories, relationships, and individual things.

For example:

<pre>
Dog → kind of → Mammal
Fido → is a → Dog
</pre>

A reasoner can infer:

<pre>
Fido → is a → Mammal
</pre>

Description logics are designed so computers can perform useful reasoning while the language remains mathematically controlled.

Different description logics allow different kinds of rules.

More expressive languages can describe more things but can also make reasoning harder.

[[Web Ontology Language/Simple|OWL]] is closely connected to description logic.

